# Chain Reaction: "deals X damage to each creature, where X is the number of creatures on the battlefield" (CR 608.2,
# 120.3). Cast on turn 3 with a Hill Giant and Bot2's Grizzly Bears out - two creatures, both players' - so X is 2: the
# 3/3 Giant takes exactly 2 and lives, the 2/2 Bears take 2 and die. Counting only Bot1's creatures would make X 1 and
# leave the Bears alive; counting the spell too would make X 3 and kill the Giant.

